Commit:     kara <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Fri Nov 20 02:14:37 2026 -0500

    gate: make both tier-1 test arms report the suite's real status
    
    Two arms claimed to gate the test suite and neither could fail on failures:
    
    - pipeline tier1 `tests` step ran `npx vitest run ... | tail -3`, so the step's
      exit code was `tail`'s (always 0). On 2026-11-20 origin/main graded PASS with
      20 failing tests in that run.
    - guards.test_command piped through `grep -q 'Tests.*passed'`, which matches
      vitest's summary line even when it reads "Tests  20 failed | 60 passed".
    
    Both now propagate vitest's own exit status; the step keeps a 20-line tail for
    triage. Red-proofed in both directions: a deliberately failing test file made
    the step exit 1 (REDPROOF_RC=1, "Tests  1 failed"), and the full suite is
    currently green at 2122 tests / 0 failed in ~32s. `gitreins config-validate`
    reports only the four pre-existing unknown-key warnings the file already
    documents.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
---
 .gitreins/config.yaml | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.gitreins/config.yaml b/.gitreins/config.yaml
index 93cac298..544d41d5 100644
--- a/.gitreins/config.yaml
+++ b/.gitreins/config.yaml
@@ -3,8 +3,10 @@ guards:
   lint: false
   allow_skips: true
   tests: true
-  test_command: npx vitest run --passWithNoTests 2>&1 | grep -q 'Tests.*passed' &&
-    exit 0 || exit 1
+  # Honest arm (2026-11-20): `grep -q 'Tests.*passed'` matched
+  # "Tests  20 failed | 60 passed", so failing runs passed this guard. Use
+  # vitest's own exit status.
+  test_command: npx vitest run --passWithNoTests
   dead_code: false
   skylos: false
   lsp: true
@@ -75,7 +77,13 @@ pipeline:
       run: bash scripts/guard-build.sh
     - id: tests
       type: script
-      run: npx vitest run --passWithNoTests 2>&1 | tail -3
+      # Honest gate (2026-11-20): the old `... | tail -3` reported the exit code
+      # of `tail`, so tier1 graded a suite with 20 failing tests as PASS. Keep
+      # the log tail for triage but propagate vitest's own status.
+      run: |
+        out=$(npx vitest run --passWithNoTests 2>&1); rc=$?
+        printf '%s\n' "$out" | tail -20
+        exit $rc
   - id: tier2
     type: ai_eval
     "on":
